RUNG 7 — tree: literally everything around a string
  Every line touching it, either side, then what touches those. No markers: contains,
  words, tower and sources are all just lines. Shows how fast the raw graph explodes.

  usage:  7-tree tomas FILE.eoe ...
          7-tree tomas --depth=3 --wide=100 FILE.eoe ...

  → x   a line from here to x        ← x   a line from x to here
  ~ x   a line about the line above  left/right   a reference, unfolded
  ↺     already shown; not grown again

branches(node):
    if node names a line:  its left end, its right end
    for each line touching node:
        the other end                          marked → or ←
        for each line about that line:  its other end, marked ~

grow(node, depth):
    kept = first --wide (12) branches
    mark every kept branch as shown before growing any    (things grow nearest the root)
    for each kept branch:
        print it, with ↺ if it was already shown
        if newly shown and depth < --depth (2):  grow(branch, depth + 1)
    if some were cut:  print "… N more"

print the string, then grow(string, 1)
